{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515269-two-clans-for-vampires","id":1515269,"title":"Two clans for Vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-16T11:15:45-07:00","id":1515269,"title":"Two clans for Vampires","content":"Anyway, just listen to this context as if it were House Rules, and let me know if that sounds feasible to you. Vampires, different from what they are in the canon, can have children from any clan, that is, if your PC is a Brujah and embraces someone, he can become a kindred from the Ventrue clan, Gangrel, Nosferatu or even a Brujah, the question is that he it can be anything, as a result of that he has the disciplines of the clan as well as their respective curse, the difference is that your parent's clan will grant him some bonuses and one more discipline among those conceived by his clan, in case you too could choose a discipline that is also your clan's to gain an evolution cost reduction: For example: If your character is from the Nosferatu clan and your parent is a Ventrue, then you can choose one of the Ventrue clan's disciplines to also be one of your clan disciplines, now if your parent is from the Brujah clan then you can select the Potence discipline and since one of the Nosferatu disciplines is already Potence then it's costs you 3 to evolve per level different from the usual 5.<br /> <br /> Other than that, the only limitation is that there are combinations that are not possible, like a Toreador cannot generate a Nosferatu, but a Nosferatu can generate a Toreador (or was it the other way around?).\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T11:36:16-07:00","id":1515273,"title":"","content":"Would sort of rip out some of the setting if you did so, requiring a different lore, but I guess you can do that. It's kinda how I do with Requiem vampires.<br /> What feedback are you looking for here, specifically? I feel like the getting in-clan disciplines cheaper thing is a bit much (especially since I'm pretty sure &quot;in-clan&quot; just means you were trained in its use starting from your first nights, as opposed to Caitiff disciplines (self-taught) or out-of-clan (outside your clan's &quot;paradigm,&quot; for lack of a better word))<br /> <br /> Like, I'm not sure you even need house rules for the general gist of it; just get creative with Caitiff characters. Most clan curses can be taken as flaws; and you absolutely can have a &quot;Nosferatu&quot; childe as a Toreador (one of my favourite character concepts in fact). Make a Toreador, slap the Monstrous flaw on them; <i>et voil\u00e0!</i> You have something the Toreador find more horrifying than a Sewer Rat. They probably also got disowned, declared Caitiff and thrown out onto the streets/made to run for their unlives from an homicidally embarrassed sire too. You can take a Toreador clan discipline, two Nosferatu disciplines and then use use your freebies to get the third.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value"